{"id": "EUVD-2026-103715", "enisaUuid": "e9bd4f7c-7dcf-3208-8b4e-1b2c52d0cd7b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/cmf: Fix virtual vs physical address confusion\n\nThe measurement block address is an absolute address. Define the\nassociated schib_config and schib fields as dma64_t to enable automatic\ndetection of incorrect assignments. Also add the missing virt_to_dma64()\ntranslation.\n\nWithout this fix, a wrong address will be used by firmware when storing\nextended format channel measurement data on kernels built with\nCONFIG_RANDOMIZE_IDENTITY_BASE=y.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b11f369be31ea11c746833e4d3ad51dcd6b5fa2b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/748ec2f7f5df9b4fc742546a8bfc8aa5d847353e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f78226eb743b362f52b212d7763801642539d1c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4d04425e66af2ecee9d1a49ae0484436f3c2fd1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98475", "GHSA-p4wm-c7q2-mpq9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0578202e-229b-39d1-8838-7fa72649f2ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "27a60219-6543-3f25-ad39-61818bd3926d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "14edd0d73bfef320fd5be11495687ba537aa6341 <7f78226eb743b362f52b212d7763801642539d1c"}, {"id": "31d117ee-4b75-3306-8568-c63018508152", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "46c0350c-4bf7-3d22-9a2f-5f678abe66d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "47cdfe06-7097-3470-9302-5484e920b4d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "ac6fd58a-fe0a-38c5-a73b-475b799b01a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {